# Build context trimming for the API image.

## Build output.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
**/.idea/
**/TestResults/
**/*.user
**/*.suo

## The legacy VB application is not part of the API image. It lives outside this build context
## (the context is AI LOGTISTICS BACKEND), so there is no pattern for it here — a ".." pattern has
## no meaning in .dockerignore and is silently ignored.

## Local overrides and secrets.
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/*.pfx
**/*.snk

## Repo furniture.
.git/
.gitignore
**/*.md
docker-compose.yml

## NOTE: NuGet.config is deliberately NOT excluded. The first restore runs before `COPY . .`, so it
## never sees this file and uses the default feed; the copy afterwards is what makes the offline
## configuration visible to later steps, which is why publish runs with --no-restore.

## NOTE: the Dockerfile itself is not excluded. Compose references it by path
## (src/Logistics.Api/Dockerfile), and an ignore pattern of `Dockerfile` would only match a file at
## the context root — excluding it here would be a silent no-op that reads like a safeguard.
